All 3 vulnerabilities in `libtiff/tif_print.c` are in `TIFFPrintDirectory()`, which is exclusively called by `tiffinfo` (with the `-c` flag) and not by `tiffsplit`. Since the only permitted trigger binary is `tiffsplit`, none of these vulnerabilities can be reached via command-line TIFF file input, and all were correctly marked SKIPPED per the rules.
